Package: phewasFlow
Type: Package
Title: Reproducible Bidirectional Phenome-Wide Association Studies
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Lars",
    family = "Fritsche",
    email = "larsf+lab@umich.edu",
    role = c("aut", "cre")
  )
Author: Lars Fritsche [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Lars Fritsche <larsf+lab@umich.edu>
URL: https://github.com/FritscheLab/phewasFlow,
    https://fritschelab.github.io/phewasFlow/,
    https://fritschelab.github.io
BugReports: https://github.com/FritscheLab/phewasFlow/issues
Description: Provides a reproducible workflow for phenome-wide association
    studies on analysis-ready phenotypes, including those constructed with
    the 'PheWAS' package. It defines explicit, validated specifications for
    scans in either direction and fits Firth logistic, linear,
    negative-binomial, and cumulative-link models; preserves skipped and
    failed associations; retains log-scale p-values through family-wide
    multiple-testing correction;
    supports deterministic local and sharded execution; and provides matched
    model contrasts, concordance summaries, and publication-ready graphics.
